lation balloon 500% in 50 years  this program is a drop in the ocean  helping only a small number of inmates  but it's an imaginative solution to help  solve the rehabilitation problem in  American prisons the incarceration issue  in in America it's obviously huge and  the difficulty is to programs like this  are really really not that easy to to  develop the aim of the wild mustang  program is to teach prisoners life  skills that will prevent them from  reoffending in the long run this will  keep the prison population down if we  can reach a handful of inmates and they  don't really not just a monetary saving  but you have a person who has now become  a productive part of society the untamed  animals show many similar traits to the  inmates and the wild these horses are  primarily focused on survival one of the  guys have come into prison have this  kind of same mindset there are so many  parallels to what what the horse goes  doing what the inmate goes through the  inmate has to learn  how to live different they have learned  how to think different the basic  principle is you make the wrong thing  harder to doing the right thing easier  to do of the 50 inmates who have been  released after completing the program  only to have returned to prison the  inmates start taking responsibility for  something beyond themselves  rehabilitation programs like this could  help break the cycle of reoffending I'm  just not the same person I was when I  first came down I don't think the same I  don't act the same I don't react the  same it's taught me to help me with  being selfless this job isn't about me  this job is about this horse right here  as I've give up my time my patience and  my energy I'm the one who's actually  being taught the lessons pioneering  programs like this a time-consuming hard  to establish and can only help a small  number of inmates but they're effective  bucking the trend of reoffending  you

